["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/nli", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Natural Location Identifier (NLI)](https://eccma.org/enli-eccma-natural-location-identifier/) is a 14- or 15-character alphanumeric string standardized by [ISO 8000-118](https://www.iso.org/standard/85428.html) that uniquely identifies a three-dimensional geographic point location. The identifier is generated from geodetic coordinates and elevation data. For electronic storage, the `ISO.NLI:` prefix shall be retained (e.g., `ISO.NLI:41TS8M-A8ELTQ-H2`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Hardware/Hardware", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:Naf359da935e046409716435a87f9bda9", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/externalRef", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRef", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vcs", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:Nc97d446a8cbe440fa51532a37a1491ed", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/runtimeAnalysisReport", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:Nf0e79b0fa62b4b52a9752cd8c7c1203e", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Dataset/dataCollectionProcess", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/from", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Element", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Business Identifier (IBID)](https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/) is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the [ISO/DIS 25500-3](https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html) draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (`|`) (e.g., `US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N2bf7d6b319134e6481e8f3c2c7f9e89c", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil", "globalId", "", ""]
